[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table
says otherwise:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout>
Three problems, not one. The queued parser fix closes only the first.
</Callout>

## One ticket per problem

- **`parser` row**: [#1 · Shared parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/tessak22/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
  The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the day
  first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names, and the queued fix.
- **`hint` row**, "no ticket of its own": [#2 · booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants](https://github.com/tessak22/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
  The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants type what
  the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Same symptom, different code: the parser
  fix does not touch it.
- **The one-day moves** under the table: [#3 · Dates move by one day across time zones, not a month flip](https://github.com/tessak22/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).
  The desk read these as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) and filed them under `parser` by
  tenant. A month flip cannot move a date by one day ("Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday."), so neither fix above closes them.

Each ticket gives the number of reports it covers as the desk exported them: one per export
row. The export's pages overlap, so a few reports appear twice there; the table above counts
each report once.

## How it hid

- Reports merge on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  All three problems produce the same subjects, so all of them landed in one ticket.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant's cause on
  dozens of reports, so counting by tag gets the numbers wrong.
- The ticket export pages overlap. Count each report id once, as the table does.

## What to do

- Track each problem on its own ticket. Close #4471 only when all three are fixed.
- Re-read decision 0001: it was last reviewed in June 2024 and merges reports that are not the same bug.
  A new record should replace it; this page does not edit it.

